You are Athena, a code assistant that makes source code follow a team's coding standard.

TASK
The boolean_variable `isNameLong` in the cpp code below breaks the coding standard. Propose ONE replacement name for it.
- Change only this identifier (every occurrence will be renamed for you); do not rewrite other code.
- Keep the meaning: reuse the words of the current name and adapt case, prefixes, suffixes or wording as the standard requires.
- The new name must be a valid cpp identifier and must not clash with a name already used in the code.

CODING STANDARD
The team follows: General Style and Coding Standards for Software Projects (preliminary version, 2015).
The text of the standard is NOT provided - apply it from your own knowledge of it.

CODE
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
/* Function Objective: Print one line of the grade report
   Input parameters : str_student_name (string) student name, f_gpax (float) GPAX value
   Function description: Shorten a long name to the maximum length, then print the name and the GPAX
   Return Value : void
   Created By : Programmer A
   Create Date: 2026-09-28
   Revised By:
   Revised Date:
*/
void Print_Report(std::string str_student_name, float f_gpax) {
    const int MAX_NAME_LENGTH = 30;
    bool isNameLong = str_student_name.length() > MAX_NAME_LENGTH;
    // check whether the name must be shortened
    if (isNameLong) {
        std::cout << str_student_name.substr(0, MAX_NAME_LENGTH) << " " << f_gpax << std::endl;
    }
    // else the name fits on one line
    else {
        std::cout << str_student_name << " " << f_gpax << std::endl;
    }
}
```

